# Tool goal

Your goal: one sentence you keep working on until it is finished. When you stop by yourself (your answer calls no tool) and no letter waits, aos puts one message in your conversation:

`[aos] goal: Fix the failing test in src/. (reminder 2 of 10. Keep working on it; ...)`

Then go on with the work, or end it. Letters always come first: a reminder comes only when your queue is empty.

```json
{"op": "get"}
{"op": "set", "text": "Fix the failing test in src/.", "limit": 10}
{"op": "done", "reason": "the test passes now"}
{"op": "done", "status": "abandoned", "reason": "the file it needs is gone"}
{"op": "pause", "reason": "waiting for bob's answer"}
{"op": "resume"}
```

- `get` -> lines `status TAB active`, `text TAB ...`, `reminded TAB 2 of 10`, `reason`, `set_by`, `updated`; or `no goal`.
- `set` replaces the goal you had and starts the count at 0. A person or your parent agent can also set, pause, resume or clear it (`aos-agent goal`, `aos/cli/goal.json`).
- When the count matters, and when to use done or pause: `aos/tools/goal.json#/rules`.

Errors: `aos/tools/goal.json#/errors`.
